N2  - Hilar cholangiocarcinoma (HCCA) is a type of bile duct cancer with insidious onset and poor prognosis. Surgical resection is the only potentially curative treatment. The selection of surgical approa-ches and prognosis assessment depend on different classification systems and preoperative imaging results. This article reviews the progress in classification systems, imaging modalities, biliary drainage teehniques, postoperative adjuvant therapy, future liver remnant insuffieieney treatment, liver transplantation and resection extent for HCCA.
