N2  - Hilar cholangiocarcinoma is a poor prognosis tumour according to its location. Preoperative examination must assess biliary, vascular, parenchymatous and lymphatic involvement. The resection of biliary convergence has to be associated to the resection of the segment I. Extension to an hepatic duct can necessitate a hepatectomy with resection of the biliary tract. Liver transplantation for hilar cholangiocarcinoma is still controversial and must be included in protocols. The prognosis is still poor and needs a multidisciplinary approach.
