N2  - Liver resection is the treatment of choice for patients with hilar cholangiocrcinoma.m In case of irresectability, liver transplantation (LT) has been proposed and is currently reassessed, due to promising data using neoadjuvant radiochemotherapy. For an increased surgical radicality, a combined hepatectomy plus pancreatic head resection (“extended bile duct resection”) has been performed during our initial experience in patients with irresectable hilar cholangiocarcinoma. The long term results (>10 y) of this cohort are analyzed to clarify the value of this procedure. Patients: 16 patients underwent hepatectomy plus Whipple's procedure followed by LT between 1992 and 1998. All patients had hilar cholangiocarcinoma in the absence of PSC. No neoadjuvant or adjuvant treatment was performed. UICC stages were I (n=6), IIA (5), II B (3) and IV (2). Preoperative CA 19-9 levels were available in 10 patients with a mean of 1748 ± 808 U/ml. Results: Overall 1, 5 and 10 yr patient survival rates were 63, 38 and 38 % respectively. 12 patients died during the follow up period, 2 due to postoperative complications, 8 due to tumor recurrence and 2 more than 10 years after transplantation (urothel carcinoma, aortic aneurysm). From the 6 patients with UICC stage I tumors only 1 patient with a preoperative CA 19-9 of 8249 U/ml developed tumor recurrence, but two died due to postoperative complications. Therefore 5 and 10 year survival was 50 % in stage I patients and not significantly higher than in UICC stage IIA (40 %) and in stage II B (33 %). The following factors showed a trend towards inferior survival: positive lymph nodes, distant metastases, high CA 19-9 levels and preoperative PTCD. Considering all lymph node negative patients after exclusion of perioperative deaths, the 10 year survival was 56 %. Conclusion: The overall long term survival was low in the reported inhomogeneous patient collective. However, using a thorough patient selection, acceptable long term results and a chance of cure could be achieved even without neoadjuvant radiochemotherapy. Owing to the increased perioperative morbidity and mortality, extended bile duct resection can not be recommended as standard procedure for irresectable hilar cholangiocarcinoma instead of LT alone.
